{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"prior-2","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py:86 `def parse_manifest_paths_by_name(text: str) -> dict[str, set[str]]:`","ABSENCE: `search_files` for `parse_manifest_paths_by_name` in tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py returned `(no matches)` — the union variant `parse_manifest_paths` has direct tests (test_parse_manifest_paths_unions_all_paths_blocks, test_parse_manifest_paths_ignores_trailing_inline_comments) but the by-name variant does not.","The `tokens = set()` reset per line at scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py:111 is the segregation logic; a regression that failed to reset would leak tokens across manifest names, silently defeating the 'require in BOTH manifests' contract without a direct test to catch it."],"finding":"The new `parse_manifest_paths_by_name` — the function that keys path tokens per `*_PATHS` manifest name and underpins the whole per-manifest cap gate — has no direct unit test. Its by-name segregation (ensuring MATERIALIZER_PATHS tokens do not leak into OBS_PATHS's set, and vice versa) is only exercised indirectly through the end-to-end RED cap test.","id":"1","impact":0.27,"location":"scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py:86","norm_id":"nadb06fea1206f152","priority":0.27,"reason":"default-advisory","standing":{"origin_decision":"advisory","origin_revision":"ef183712a82746ff5517695c17d6ecbfd754fccc","state":"still-present"},"suggested_fix":"Add: `def test_parse_manifest_paths_by_name_segregates_tokens():` asserting `gate.parse_manifest_paths_by_name(\"A_PATHS='x/1 x/2'\\nB_PATHS='y/1'\\n\") == {'A_PATHS': {'x/1','x/2'}, 'B_PATHS': {'y/1'}}`.","tie